cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, or the technique it documents, please cite it as below."
title: "HP ProLiant ML10 Gen9 - Graphics / Display Fix (Linux, Windows Server & more)"
abstract: >-
  Root-cause analysis and a tested fix for the blank / no-signal display on the
  HPE ProLiant ML10 Gen9, whose onboard Intel HD Graphics P530 (Skylake) fails
  over a passive DisplayPort -> DVI -> HDMI adapter chain because the adapter
  hides the monitor's EDID (the GMBUS read fails and the output is never
  enabled). Includes a portable Linux bootloader toolkit for GRUB and
  systemd-boot, Windows and Windows Server driver/tooling plus a native
  DisplayFix.exe, a FreeBSD helper, hardware/cable guidance, verification and
  full troubleshooting.
